{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-118556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The population $y(t)$ of chimpanzees in a Brazilian forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(1-\\frac{y}{500}),\\,y(0)=70,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible chimpanzee population?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-118556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(1-\\frac{y}{500}) \\\\  & =y(\\frac{500-y}{500}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{500}(500-y) \\\\  & =0.002y(500-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=500.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $500,$ and we conclude that the number of chimpanzees cannot exceed $500.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-118556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "795f4f5bed08e985d78648192099113062117e4addf5fb313fbec0a9358b1e91"} {"question" "q-118556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-118556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1\\,000"] ["math" "430"] ["math" "500"] ["math" "570"] ["math" "700"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-118556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "500"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-119854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The rate of growth in the number of plants $P(t)$ infected with a pest in a certain land follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.5P-0.0025{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=5.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in months. For which value of $P$ is the number of plants infected with the pest growing at the fastest possible rate?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-119854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.5P-0.0025{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.0025P(200-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=200.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $200,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 200=100.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-119854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "795f4f5bed08e985d78648192099113062117e4addf5fb313fbec0a9358b1e91"} {"question" "q-119854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-119854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "100"] ["math" "200"] ["math" "250"] ["math" "400"] ["math" "50"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-119854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "100"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-348209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The population $y(t)$ of giraffes on a certain African wildlife reserve follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=14.4y-0.003{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=150,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible population of giraffes?\n\nThe maximum possible population of giraffes is\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-348209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/d8133f1c4203903bac606bbae61c73717e2ba2dc15a97a77f48eaaeaf4736d06.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =14.4y-0.003{y}^{2} \\\\  & =0.003y(4800-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=4800.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $4800,$ and we conclude that the maximum possible population of giraffes is $4800.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-348209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "795f4f5bed08e985d78648192099113062117e4addf5fb313fbec0a9358b1e91"} {"question" "q-348209" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-348209" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4800"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The download count $P(t)$ of a viral mobile game follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=4P(8\\,000-P),\\,P(0)=600.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the download count growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFrom our equation, we see that $a=8000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $8000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8000=4000.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "795f4f5bed08e985d78648192099113062117e4addf5fb313fbec0a9358b1e91"} {"question" "q-353483" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353483" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4000"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The number $P(t)$ of stores in a retail chain follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=6300P-7{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=50,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the number of stores growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =6300P-7{P}^{2} \\\\  & =7P(900-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=900.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $900,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 900=450.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "795f4f5bed08e985d78648192099113062117e4addf5fb313fbec0a9358b1e91"} {"question" "q-353490" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"} {"question" "q-353490" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "450"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2e78f45ba74f9e82dc8117ef1e422dc404f0fbff673e677d393a19ded2e373e"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2587 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
